# Console UX — product quality bar

Design and implement the console like a **polished consumer product** (ChatGPT, Linear, Stripe Dashboard). Prioritize clarity, calm visuals, and trust. When in doubt, remove noise.

## Visual language

- **Quiet chrome, loud content** — sidebar and header stay neutral; conversation and data are the focus.
- **Generous whitespace** — `max-w-3xl` centered chat column; avoid full-bleed text walls.
- **Rounded, soft surfaces** — `rounded-2xl` bubbles; `rounded-xl` cards; no harsh boxes.
- **Typography hierarchy** — body `text-sm`; labels `text-xs text-muted-foreground`; one weight step for emphasis, not three.
- **Color with purpose** — primary for user messages only; assistant on `bg-muted`; errors amber (recoverable), destructive red (fatal). Never decorate with color.
- **Dark mode first-class** — test both themes; contrast must pass without glowing borders.

## Chat layout (ChatGPT pattern)

```
[scrollable message area — flex-1, overflow-y-auto]
[optional error strip — one line, above composer]
[composer pinned bottom — full width of column, not viewport]
```

- Empty state: one short line + subtle hint, centered — no illustrations unless requested.
- User bubble: right-aligned, `bg-primary`, max ~85% width.
- Assistant: left-aligned, `bg-muted`, answer text first.
- **Evidence below answer** — tool/source cards inside the assistant block, separated by `border-t`, labeled “Based on your data”. Never interleave cards between user and answer.
- Loading: single “Thinking…” bubble — no spinners everywhere.
- Composer: textarea grows to ~4 lines; Enter sends, Shift+Enter newline; disabled state while pending.

## Grounded finance UX

- **Never show raw API/Go errors** — map to plain language; keep JSON in collapsed “Technical details”.
- **Human tool names** — “Spending summary”, not `get_cashflow`.
- **Show the period** — always render the date range from tool input so users can spot model mistakes.
- **Empty ≠ error** — “No outgoing payments in this period” is a valid outcome; don’t imply failure.
- **One primary action per card** — “View transactions” with pre-filled filters; secondary “Open” per merchant row only when useful.
- **Progressive disclosure** — summary metrics visible; raw tool payload hidden in `<details>`.

## Interaction

- Links to `/transactions` must preserve filter state in URL (shareable, back-button safe).
- Click targets ≥ 44px where possible; visible focus rings (`focus-visible:ring`).
- Prefer `Link` (TanStack Router) over `window.location` for in-app navigation.
- Disable composer during flight; no duplicate sends.

## Content and tone

- UI copy: short, confident, no jargon (“Top counterparties”, not “tool invocation”).
- Assistant answers are the product; UI labels support, never compete.
- Format money consistently: `{amount} {currency}` tabular nums.

## Anti-patterns (reject in review)

- Raw error strings, stack traces, or `json:` blobs in the main UI
- Multiple competing CTAs in one card
- Tool names or snake_case in user-visible text
- Full-width JSON debug panels by default
- Modal dialogs for drill-down when a sheet or linked page suffices
- Breaking layout shift when evidence cards appear — reserve min spacing

